From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Subject: [PATCH] assoc: mark clients absent from the live monitor inactive

The full associated-client data model can retain an authorized station after
it silently roams to another AP.  The live monitor map is refreshed from the
HAL and no longer contains that station, but get_sta_stats_info() returned an
error without invalidating the cached cli_Active value.  A subsequent full
list therefore continued to advertise the stale association as active.

Mark the cached entry inactive when it has no corresponding live monitor
entry.  Keep the entry itself so a transiently unavailable monitor cannot
destroy association history and a later successful refresh can make it active
again.  The full-list encoder can now distinguish a live snapshot entry from
retained history.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 source/stats/wifi_monitor.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/source/stats/wifi_monitor.c b/source/stats/wifi_monitor.c
--- a/source/stats/wifi_monitor.c
+++ b/source/stats/wifi_monitor.c
@@ -1508,6 +1508,7 @@ int get_sta_stats_info (assoc_dev_data_t *assoc_dev_data) {
 
     sta_data = (sta_data_t *)hash_map_get(sta_map, sta_key);
     if (sta_data == NULL) {
+        assoc_dev_data->dev_stats.cli_Active = false;
         wifi_util_error_print(WIFI_MON, "%s:%d: NULL pointer\n", __func__, __LINE__);
         pthread_mutex_unlock(&g_monitor_module.data_lock);
         return -1;
